asm2dbsm2 — License and Upstream Agreement Notice

This package contains Python modules adapted from BSM2 and BSM2-GHG Matlab implementations and refactored for ASM2d-compatible Python use.

This package is provided under the upstream acknowledgement described below.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Upstream BSM2 Agreement Notice
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The BSM2 implementations by:

• *Benchmark Simulation Model No 2 (BSM2)* Ulf Jeppsson and Christian Rosen. Department of Industrial Electrical Engineering and Automation (IEA), Lund University, Lund, Sweden, and the IWA Task Group on Benchmarking of Control Strategies for WWTPs. 2009/2011.

• *Benchmarking biological nutrient removal in wastewater treatment plants: influence of mathematical model assumptions*. Xavier Flores-Alsina, Krist V. Gernaey and Ulf Jeppsson. 2012. https://iwaponline.com/wst/article-abstract/65/8/1496/14436/Benchmarking-biological-nutrient-removal-in?redirectedFrom=fulltext 

• *Balancing effluent quality, economic cost and greenhouse gas emissions during the evaluation of (plant-wide) control/operational strategies in WWTPs* Xavier Flores-Alsina, Magnus Arnell, Youri Amerlinck, Lluís Corominas, Krist V. Gernaey, Lisha Guo, Erik Lindblom, Ingmar Nopens, Jose Porro, Andy Shaw, Laura Snip, Peter A. Vanrolleghem, and Ulf Jeppsson. 2014. https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0048969713008140


The upstream notice requests users to:

• send feedback if errors, improvements, or unusual operational behaviour are found;
• send copies of scientific papers that are based to some extent on the model implementations;
• acknowledge the work carried out by Lund University, PROSYS DTU, and the relevant upstream authors in publications where the use of the implementations has had an impact.

